        "question_arQhrK": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How are Frood products high fibre?",
            "answer": "<p>Frood products are naturally high in fibre due to their ingredient composition. Across the range, recipes include<br/><br/><br/>Dehydrated vegetables such as carrot, tomato, onion, peppers and spinach</p><p>Plant-based ingredients like wholegrain oats, linseed, and faba bean protein</p><p>Herbs and spices, which also contribute small amounts of fibre</p><p>These ingredients result in fibre levels typically ranging from around 12g to 17g per 100g (dry product) across the range.</p><p>Fibre plays an important role in digestive health and can also help you feel fuller for longer.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_eTfDHz": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What accreditations do your manufacturers products hold?",
            "answer": "<p>Our manufacturing partner operates to high food safety and quality standards and holds a BRCGS (Brand Reputation Compliance Global Standards) Food Safety certification at AA+ grade, which is the highest rating available and achieved through unannounced audits.<br/><br/>In addition, the site holds a number of recognised certifications and standards, including:</p><ul><li>RSPO (Roundtable on Sustainable Palm Oil)</li><li>Halal certification</li><li>SEDEX / SMETA (ethical trade and supply chain standards)</li><li>Gluten Free certification and controls</li><li>Compliance with FSMA (Food Safety Modernization Act) standards</li></ul><p>These accreditations ensure strong controls across food safety, quality, sustainability, and ethical practices.</p>"
          }
        },
